artifact.self_contained_problem:
Let (K, v) be a valued field with valuation ring O_K, value group vK, and residue field Kv. Call (K, v) extremal if for every n ≥ 1 and every polynomial f(X_1, …, X_n) ∈ K[X_1, …, X_n], the set
  { v(f(a_1, …, a_n)) : a_1, …, a_n ∈ O_K } ⊆ vK ∪ {∞}
attains a maximum.

A valuation w on K is called a coarsening of v if the valuation ring of w contains the valuation ring of v (equivalently, every v-open set is w-open). Given such a coarsening w with residue field Kw, the valuation v induces a valuation w̄ on Kw whose valuation ring is O_K / m_w (where m_w is the maximal ideal of the valuation ring of w). One writes v = w ∘ w̄ and calls v the composition of w and w̄; the residue field of (Kw, w̄) is canonically identified with Kv.

Question: Suppose that (K, v) admits a decomposition v = w ∘ w̄ such that:
 (i) the value group wK is divisible;
 (ii) the valued field (K, w) is extremal;
 (iii) the valued field (Kw, w̄) is extremal.

Does it follow that (K, v) is extremal?

